program switch_case_locals

? Regression: a C switch case body starting with a local declaration used to
? emit `case X:` followed directly by the declaration, which is not valid C
? (a label may only precede a statement). Case bodies now get their own
? braces, so a declaration can open a case.

@ label_for |k:int| string:
	switch k:
		on 1:
			one_part: "one"
			return one_part
		on 2, 3:
			few_part: "few"
			return few_part
		_: return "many"
	$
$

@ main ||:
	expected: []

	a: string = label_for|1|
	print|a|
	expected.push|"one"|

	b: string = label_for|2|
	print|b|
	expected.push|"few"|

	c: string = label_for|9|
	print|c|
	expected.push|"many"|

	print|expected|
$
